  "content": "The structure is built and saved.\n\n**Molecule:** reserpine \u2013 the pentacyclic indole alkaloid shown, i.e. methyl 11,17\u2011dimethoxy\u201118\u2011(3,4,5\u2011trimethoxybenzoyloxy)\u2011yohimban\u201116\u2011carboxylate, C\u2083\u2083H\u2084\u2080N\u2082O\u2089 (84 atoms including all hydrogens).\n\n**How it was built**\n1. Transcribed the drawing into a mol block using the 2D atom positions and the wedge/hash bonds exactly as depicted (H at C3 wedged, H at C15 hashed, CO\u2082Me at C16 wedged, OMe at C17 hashed, benzoate O at C18 wedged, H at C20 hashed), so RDKit assigned all six stereocentres directly from the picture.\n2. Generated 3D conformers (ETKDG + MMFF), took the lowest-energy one, and then optimised it with GFN2\u2011xTB.\n3. Re-perceived the stereochemistry from the final 3D coordinates and confirmed it is identical to what the drawing encodes:\n   `COC(=O)[C@H]1[C@H]2C[C@@H]3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3C[C@H]2C[C@@H](OC(=O)c2cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c2)[C@@H]1OC`\n\n**Confirmation:** `answer.xyz` exists in the working directory (84 atoms, standard XYZ format, \u00c5, right-handed coordinates, all explicit hydrogens included).",
